[chunk 1/1] FILING ANALYSIS: Adobe 10-K (FY2024, filed 2025-01-13). Item 3 (Legal Proceedings) is boilerplate reference to Note 16. Item 5-7 contain MD&A with business operations and financial results. SIFI-MATERIAL FINDINGS: (1) CAPEX_ROI_GAP signal: Adobe disclosed $5.79B in non-cancellable unconditional purchase obligations (primarily third-party hosting and data center services) with $463M in operating lease obligations through 2034, but revenue is subscription-based (95% of $21.5B = $20.5B) with high gross margins (89% on subscription). Infrastructure spend is matched to operations but worth monitoring for scale efficiency. (2) COST_OPACITY: Significant AI training/inferencing cost embedded in R&D ($3.944B, +14% YoY) and hosting/data center costs (mentioned across cost of revenue, R&D, and SG&A) but NOT separately disclosed by amount—only noted as components. This creates opacity on Adobe's actual compute spend and AI scaling costs. (3) FIGMA ACQUISITION FAILURE: $1B termination fee incurred in FY2024 (disclosed in Item 7 MD&A, Operating Expenses). This is a material non-recurring charge but NOT classified as a hidden risk because it is fully disclosed and settled. No circularity or off-balance-sheet leverage involved. (4) CASH POSITION & LIQUIDITY: $7.613B cash + $273M short-term investments as of 2024-11-29; $1.5B revolving credit agreement undrawn; $3B commercial paper program undrawn. Senior notes: $5.65B outstanding (includes $1.5B due Feb 1, 2025, to be refinanced). No solvency concerns. NO SIFI-MATERIAL HIDDEN LEVERAGE, CIRCULARITY, or REVENUE ROUNDTRIP identified in this section. Adobe is a mature, profitable SaaS company with subscription dominance and standard operating leases. The Figma deal failure is disclosed; no undisclosed SPVs or VIEs mentioned."
